+- [x] 1.2 Add `CouponRepository.recordRedemption(orderId, couponCode, discountCents, createdAt)` and `CouponRepository.incrementUsedCount(code)`; verify with `npm run build`.
+
+## 2. Apply-coupon service rules
+
+- [x] 2.1 Implement `OrderService.applyCoupon(id, couponCode)` in `src/services/orderService.ts`: reject a missing/blank code (`INVALID_REQUEST`), an unknown coupon (`COUPON_NOT_FOUND`), a non-`ACTIVE` coupon (`COUPON_INACTIVE`), a coupon outside its `validFrom`/`validUntil` window (`COUPON_NOT_YET_VALID` / `COUPON_EXPIRED`), an order below `minAmountCents` (`COUPON_MIN_AMOUNT`) and a reached `usageLimit` (`COUPON_USAGE_LIMIT_REACHED`), all as HTTP 400; then compute the discount, update the order and record the redemption. Verify with `npm run build`.
+- [x] 2.2 Inject `CouponRepository` (and keep the `Clock`) into `OrderService` in `src/app.ts`; verify with `npm run build` and `npm test`.
+- [x] 2.3 Add `tests/apply-coupon.test.ts` covering the validation rules (unknown, disabled, expired, not-yet-valid, below minimum) using a fixed clock and `createApp`; verify with `npm test`.
+- [x] 2.4 Add cases to `tests/apply-coupon.test.ts` for a `FIXED` discount, a `PERCENT` discount, the `maxDiscountCents` cap and the discount-never-exceeds-amount clamp; verify with `npm test`.
+
+## 3. HTTP route
+
+- [x] 3.1 Register `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` in `src/routes/orders.ts` returning HTTP 200 with the updated order and HTTP 400 for invalid coupons; verify with an integration case in `tests/apply-coupon.test.ts` asserting status 200 and the updated `discountCents`/`finalAmountCents`/`couponCode`.
+- [x] 3.2 Verify an unknown order id still yields 404 `ORDER_NOT_FOUND` and that the existing order routes are unaffected; verify with `npm test`.
+
+## 4. Verification
+
+- [x] 4.1 Run `npm run build` and `npm test` on the full suite and confirm all tests pass, including the untouched `tests/orders.test.ts`.
+
+## Workflow follow-up
+
+- Archive the change once the project's review requirements are satisfied.
